&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;as deemed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;22.7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; million in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; and $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;7.4 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;million in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; and was included within Other Paid-in Capital in the Comparative Balance Sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;We will make all necessary adjustments to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;account&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; balances upon a ruling in Docket No. AC18-227-000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the United States enacted the &amp;#8220;Tax Cuts and Jobs Act&amp;#8221; (&amp;#8220;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;TCJA &amp;#8221;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;). The changes in the TCJA are effective for taxation years beginning after December 31, 2017. While the changes are broad and complex, the most significant change is the reduction in the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. We recorded a $90.2 million decrease to our 2017 deferred income tax liability, a $29.9 million increase to our 2017 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting increase of $120.1 million to our regulatory liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;In 2018 pursuant to guidance established in FERC Docket No. PL19-2-000, we began amortizing the regulated liability utilizing the reverse South Georgia flowback methodology over the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;51.6 year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; remaining life of the assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;In 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;, we recorded a $2.3 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $0.6 million decrease to our 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; deferred income tax &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; and an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;offsetting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; $1.7 million benefit to our 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; deferred federal tax expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;In 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;, we recorded a $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;2.3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; million decrease to regulatory liability, a $0.6 million decrease to our 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $1.7 million benefit to our 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt;"&gt; deferred federal tax expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; color: #ffffff;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In the normal course of business, SEP and its affiliates perform centralized corporate functions for us, including legal, accounting, compliance, treasury and other areas. We have Service Agreements with affiliates of both Spectra Energy and Enable (collectively, our members). Pursuant to the terms of the Service Agreements, all authorized costs, including labor, administrative and general, and overhead costs, incurred by our members in performing operations on our behalf are reimbursed by us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
